:"Colorado Buffaloes players says the return of head coach Deion Sanders following his recent battle with bladder cancer has been \"a breath of fresh air.\"","published":"2025-08-01T11:45:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/45862667/deion-sanders-return-breath-fresh-air-colorado-players","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Anger Index: Why Texas Tech, Tennessee and the Group of 6 should be mad","description":"Ranking the teams who should be most upset about their latest CFP ranking.","published":"2026-11-18T04:25:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510905/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-texas-tech","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Michigan to hire Texas A&M's Trev Alberts as athletic director","description":"Michigan has reached a deal to hire Texas A&M athletic director Trev Alberts to replace the departing Warde Manuel, sources told ESPN on Tuesday.","published":"2026-11-18T03:43:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50516550/michigan-hire-texas-trev-alberts-athletic-director","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on College Football Playoff bubble after the committee's third ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-18T03:42:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's third top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's third set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:34:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514170/cfp-2026-third-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest surges into CFP top 12; top 4 unchanged while Texas jumps Notre Dame","description":"Alabama stayed at No. 3 despite some struggles on Saturday while two-loss Texas jumped one-loss Notre Dame for No. 5 in the CFP's latest rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:55:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50515993/wake-forest-surges-cfp-top-12-texas-jumps-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pawn shop fighting 'Gold Digger' trademark filed by Jordon Hudson's company","description":"A California pawn shop is opposing a trademark application for \"Gold Digger\" filed by a company connected to Jordan Hudson, then-companion of Bill Belichick.","published":"2026-11-18T00:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50514442/pawn-shop-fights-gold-digger-trademark-filed-hudson","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Anthony Olivieri","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4707184/dj-mckinney","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJ_McKinney"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"DJ McKinney","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJ_McKinney","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:46Z","intro":"Dylahn Jordan McKinney (born February 9, 2004) is an American college football cornerback for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Oklahoma State Cowboys and Colorado Buffaloes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McKinney attended Colleyville Heritage High School in Colleyville, Texas. He had 43 tackles and two interceptions his junior year and 35 tackles and five interceptions as a senior. He committed to Oklahoma State University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"McKinney played at Oklahoma State in 2022 and 2023. After redshirting his first year in 2022, he played in all 14 games in 2023 and had 38 tackles. After the season, McKinney entered the transfer portal and transferred to the University of Colorado Boulder. In his first year at Colorado in 2024, he started all 13 games and had 62 tackles, three interceptions and one interception returned for a touchdown. McKinney returned in 2025, where he played nine games and had 35 tackles, one interception, and five pass breakups. At the end of the season, McKinney entered the transfer portal and transferred to Notre Dame."}]}}